{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>If you will surely hear.</b> This is an acceptance they accepted upon themselves." "<b>You shall do.</b> This is action." "<b>And you will hearken.</b> You will incline the ear to be precise in them." "<b>All His statutes.</b> Matters that are nothing but a decree of the King, without any reason, and the evil inclination taunts over them: What prohibition is in these? Why were they forbidden? Such as wearing kilayim and eating pork and the red heifer and the like (Yoma 67)." "<b>I will put none upon you.</b> And if I do put — it is as though none was put; <b>for I am YHWH your healer</b> — this is its midrash. And according to its plain sense: for I am YHWH your healer, and I teach you Torah and commandments so that you will be saved from them — like a doctor who says to a person: do not eat this thing lest it bring you to this illness. And so it says: ״רִפְאוּת תְּהִי לְשָׁרֶּךָ״ (Proverbs 3)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:35.422200440Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}